 34S  c  1985Al03,1986Al21: {+34}S(n,n),(n,n') with 21.7 and 25.5-MeV monoenergetic neutrons produced via the 3H(d,n)4He reaction using a pulsed and bunched deuteron beam at the Ohio University Beam Swinger time-of-flight facility.
 
The target was 93.6% and 94.5%-enriched      
 34S 2c  {+34}S powder. Scattered neutrons were detected utilizing a seven-fold array of NE213 liquid scintillation detectors. Measured |s(E{-n},|q) and deduced what using coupled-channels (CC) analysis anharmonic vibrational (AHV) collective model.
 
 Probably used same experimental device as that described by     
 34S 2c  1986Al21 (FWHM=400 keV). Measured angular distributions and coupled    
 34S 2c  channels calculations (code ECIS)                                      
 34S  c  1986Al21: {+34}S(n,n),(n,n') E=21.7, 25.5 MeV, target of 94.5%-enriched
 34S 2c  {+34}S. Used seven-fold array of liquid scintillator detectors         
 34S 2c  (FWHM=450 keV). Measured angular distributions and coupled channels    
 34S 2c  calculations (code ECIS)                                               
